course: dictionary
lesson: 78
title: One word, many meanings: act
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. Act is a good example. «Act fast» means do something quickly, as in an emergency. «Stop acting silly» means behave in a certain way. It is the same word, but the meaning changes with the context.
explain: Look for clues near the word. Words like play, stage or film point to acting in a show. Words like fast, kind or silly point to doing something or behaving in a certain way. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Act can also be a noun, meaning a thing someone does. «One kind act, like bringing soup to someone ill, can end a feud.» Here an act is a single deed. A feud is a long, bitter quarrel between people, and the kind act helps to end it.
fact: Act can be a verb (to act, acts, acted, acting) or a noun (an act, acts).
fact: «Act fast» means do the right thing quickly, such as getting an adult or calling for help.
fact: In a play, actors act, and the play is divided into acts and scenes.
fact: «An act of kindness» means one thing someone does that is kind.
fact: An Act with a capital A is a law made by a parliament or congress.
exercise: «If you think a friend has stolen something, you have a duty to act.» What does act mean here? | *Do something about it | Sit down and wait quietly | Pretend you did not see | Go to sleep
exercise: «Stop acting silly.» What does acting mean here? | Making a new law | *Behaving in a certain way | Playing a part in a show | Running very fast
exercise: «One kind act, like bringing soup to someone ill, can end a feud.» What is an act in this sentence? | A short show by a performer | *A thing someone does | A law made by parliament | A part of a play
test: In «Act quickly in an emergency», which word is a verb? | *act | emergency | in | quickly
test: «The Act was passed by parliament last year.» What does Act mean here? | *A law | To behave in a silly way | A part of a play | A deed or kind thing
exam: «The play has three acts and a short final scene.» Which meaning of act fits here? | A kind deed | To do something quickly | *A part of a play | A law made by parliament
